## v0.25.8

### v9 transaction authorization — Phase 1 (shadow mode), unsigned-import fix

Background: the unsigned-transaction import hole confirmed earlier was worse
than replay-only — served transactions carried no top-level signature, so
followers and attesters applied block transactions without ever verifying
them, at every version. A single compromised validator key could propose a
block draining any account: attesters sign header fields only, and the
mempool-side admission checks are a proposer's own choice.

Phase 1 ships the v9 machinery inactive (state_transition_v9_height unset):

- Shared policy in aitbc_chain/state/v9_policy.py: V9_UNSIGNED_ALLOWED_TX_TYPES
  = {BRIDGE_LOCK, BRIDGE_RELEASE, BRIDGE_REFUND, MESSAGE} — the only types
  legitimately unsigned today (bridge rows are authority-signed or debited
  at request time; MESSAGE is a zero-value internal write). One list feeds
  both apply paths and remote attestation so the rule cannot drift.
- Apply gates (sequential + parallel): a non-allowlisted tx without a
  signature logs and counts v9_would_reject_total plus
  v9_would_reject_missing_signature_<type>_total, then applies as before —
  shadow mode. At v9 activation the same check rejects. A tx that does carry
  a signature is verified as today (v7+ check unchanged).
- /rpc/blocks-range now serves the stored signed envelope as the transaction
  body (signature digests cover the exact submitted field set, so only the
  digest-excluded tx_hash and value alias are added); rows predating
  envelope persistence keep the legacy column dump. /rpc/block/{height}
  hoists envelope.signature into its served shape. Gossip block pushes
  already carried the signed mempool envelope; /rpc/sync state exports ship
  the envelope column verbatim. A follower re-serving a block it imported
  now preserves the signature hop-to-hop.
- Remote attestation: requests carry the block's signed transaction
  envelopes; the service gained a session_factory and checks, before
  signing, that it sits at the block's parent (else refuses at v9), that
  every non-allowlisted tx carries a valid signature, and that nonce order
  is sequential per sender (unsigned internals still advance the counter —
  BRIDGE_LOCK/MESSAGE bump the sender nonce at apply). Oversized requests
  (> gossip_max_message_size) are refused. While v9 is inactive a failed
  check counts v9_would_reject_attest_<reason>_total and the attestation
  still goes out; at v9 it refuses.
- Proposer plumbing: _run_consensus_gates/_collect_and_gate_attestations/
  _collect_attestations thread the signed envelopes into the request;
  _reapply_parent_block rebuilds tx_data from the stored envelope when one
  exists, so a v9 parent re-applies with its signature intact.
- fleet-config-check now compares STATE_TRANSITION_V9_HEIGHT.

Phase 2 (after shadow counters stay clean on live traffic): pin
state_transition_v9_height in config.py like v4-v8, deploy via the rejoin
runbook, confirm every validator reports the same effective height before
the chain reaches it, then watch v9_would_reject_total as a real rejection
count and [PROPOSE] success for the first several hundred blocks.

Blocks before v9 cannot be re-verified for transaction authorization —
their signatures were never stored or served. Trust in pre-v9 history is
anchored by checkpoints, not by re-validation.


### v9 follow-ups: signed BRIDGE_LOCK, MESSAGE off the allowlist, envelope hoist (2026-09-28)

- Envelope-serving replay proof: all 8 enveloped transactions since height
  26722 verify with verify_transaction_signature over the exact body
  /rpc/blocks-range now serves after import normalisation (from/to/value
  added) — 8/8 on hub and node1. node0 had one row (height 26881,
  0xcf2282eaaa89) stored in the pre-fix nested shape (empty top-level
  signature, signed envelope under "envelope"); repaired in place after a
  DB-file backup (chain.db.bak-20260928-envhoist) and the hoist hardening
  added: _served_tx_body and _append_block normalisation both lift a nested
  signed envelope when the top level carries none, so the shape can neither
  be served nor imported unsigned again.
- V9_UNSIGNED_ALLOWED_TX_TYPES is now exactly
  {BRIDGE_LOCK, BRIDGE_RELEASE, BRIDGE_REFUND}: MESSAGE is gone — no
  internal producer creates it and it increments the sender nonce at apply,
  so an unsigned forged MESSAGE was a nonce-DoS against any account.
- BRIDGE_LOCK now carries the bridge authority's bridge_signature over its
  semantic fields (bridge_lock_message/sign_bridge_lock/
  verify_bridge_lock_signature in state/bridge_credit.py, mirroring the v5
  credit rule); initiate_transfer signs with bridge_credit_private_key() on
  both the mempool dict and the pre-registered row payload. Verified on both
  apply paths (validate_transaction and the parallel delta) and by remote
  attesters from v9 (refusals bridge_authority_unset /
  bridge_signature_missing / bridge_signature_invalid). Below the v9 height
  an unsigned lock still applies — historical replay is full of them — and
  counts v9_would_reject_bridge_lock_unsigned_total.
- Faucet finding: hub's aitbc-agent-coordinator has had NO
  GENESIS_PRIVATE_KEY in any env file (confirmed against the 26-Sep
  pre-strip backup), so /api/v1/agent/coin-requests/*/execute has returned
  503 since before the key confinement; last successful execute was
  2026-09-09. hub1's agent-coordinator DID hold the proposer key via
  node.env/blockchain-secrets.env until the 28-Sep strip. Decision: leave
  the faucet fail-closed until it gets its own funded wallet (key-split
  work) — the proposer key is not being re-added.
- Prometheus rules: V9ShadowRejection (increase(v9_would_reject_total[10m]))
  and V9AttestationRefusal (v9_would_reject_attest_*_total) added to the
