### Incident 2026-09-28: fleet wedge at 27207 during v9 canary run

Timeline (UTC): 21:59:14 hub applies canary GPU_MARKETPLACE 0xf263f881e54f
in block 27207 (recorded root 0xb67f4cbe…). 21:59:16–17 hub's own sync
manager runs "delta sync from https://<sync-source>.aitbc.bubuit.net 27205→27206"
and logs "1 accounts changed, state root matches" — matching block 27206's
root, which is exactly the problem: the delta overwrote the canary
account's committed 27207 state with its 27206 state. 22:00:24 hub and
hub1 (which pulled the same delta from hub) log "Local state diverged from
our own head 27207 … BLOCK REJECTED". node0/node1/node2 had imported 27207
correctly and produced empty 27208/27209 (root 0xb67f); ~22:03 they pulled
hub's /rpc/state/snapshot (59 accounts, root 0xc7f9b455… = 27206 state,
updated=1) and accepted it because it matched the source's claimed root,
not their own head's recorded state_root. All five nodes ended up diverged
from their recorded heads; production stopped at 27209 (~22:02) for ~1 h.

Cause — two defects, neither v9-related:
- hub /etc/aitbc/node.env CHAIN_SYNC_SOURCES=…:https://hub1… plus
  AUTO_SYNC_ENABLED made the PROPOSER run follower state sync from the
  demoted follower every ~5 min (34 runs in the prior 3 h); the two-second
  race with its own block apply lost the block's state delta.
- Snapshot/delta application was validated against the source's claimed
  root, never the local head's recorded root, and the delta path committed
  before checking then "fell back" on mismatch — the poison path.
The v9 counters only reported the consequence (not_at_parent on hub/hub1).

Repair (operator-approved, executed verbatim): all aitbc-blockchain-node
and -rpc services stopped fleet-wide; chain.db backed up
(chain.db.bak-20260928-27207wedge) on all five; single-row
UPDATE account SET balance=179855999, nonce=4 for
0xF4924759508E420eeD947BD33326731B11c4B7Df (derived from the 27207 tx:
value 1 + fee 36000 on the 27206 before-image 179891999/3 from the
block_state_delta journal; self-send so net −36000, fee burned) — 1 row on
each host; blocks 27208/27209 + bridge_block_header rows copied from node1
into hub/hub1 (hub's bbh ids autoincremented 18969/18970);
compute_state_root_full = 0xb67f4cbe2a1da8b0bae07632aabdd6b59138cc9661716fa27a0a1998127c8c6b
on all five before restart; Redis account caches held no entries for the
address; hub CHAIN_SYNC_SOURCES commented out; STATE_SYNC_MAX_GAP=-1 set on
all five (periodic delta/snapshot state sync disabled until this fix is
deployed); hub started first, then followers; converged at 27212 and
producing; the dropped GPU_ALLOCATE canary was re-submitted and sealed at
27213 (0x0ad9a26fb54a…, canary nonce 5).

Code fix in this commit (apps/blockchain-node):
- config.is_block_producer() is now the single definition of "this node
  produces blocks" (hub mode or configured PBFT validator); main.py uses
  it for the producer gate instead of an inline copy.
- StateSyncMixin refuses any state sync on a producer before any network
  call (reason block_producer); sync_manager._chain_loop also skips the
  STATE_SYNC branch on producers (bulk block import unchanged).
- delta_sync_from reads the local head first: to_height < head →
  stale_target; to_height > head → ahead_of_local_head (block import must
  catch up; no snapshot fallback); only to_height == head proceeds. The
  diff's claimed to_state_root must equal the head's recorded root
  (source_root_disagrees). Changes apply, flush, and are root-checked
  against the local recorded root in the SAME session before commit —
  mismatch → rollback, root_mismatch_local_head, nothing persisted.
- sync_state_from keeps the gap/divergence skips, refuses a snapshot whose
  claimed root differs from the local head root before writing anything
  (source_root_disagrees), and applies/validates/commits the same way.
- Every refusal increments state_sync_refused_total and
  state_sync_refused_<reason>_total.
- tests/test_state_sync_guards.py: 8 cases covering producer refusal (no
  network), stale/ahead targets, source-root disagreement, and
  rollback-before-commit for both paths.

Pre-existing finding recorded during the side-table digest
(node2:/tmp/wedge-repair/aux_divergence.txt): non-account chain tables
already diverge across hosts — escrow 45/27/44/27/45
(hub/hub1/node0/node1/node2), governance_vote 5/5/5/5/10,
cross_chain_transfer 4/0/0/0/4, cross_chain_swap 1/0/0/0/1,
bridge_validators 6/0/2/2/6; gpu_allocation, governance_proposal, and
stake semantic digests differ; bridge_block_header has duplicate-height
rows on node0 (+2) and node2 (+3). The account-only state root cannot see
any of this; it feeds the fork-journal/orphan-detection work.

The v9 shadow window restarts when this fix is deployed fleet-wide; the
v9 counters were not at fault, but the fleet was down during the window.
STATE_SYNC_MAX_GAP=-1 stays in place until the operator re-enables
periodic state sync.

