  once on the control host so every node digests the same classification even
  mid-deploy; fleet-config-check.sh carries an embedded fallback kept in
  parity by tests/test_fleet_digest_spec.py.
- scripts/monitoring/state-digest-remote.py is a stdlib-only read-only helper
  piped to each host: volatile columns (id, *_at, timestamps, autoincrement
  keys) excluded, addresses lowercased, JSON envelopes normalized
  (tx_hash/value/chain_id re-echoes and falsy signature dropped), sorted
  row-hash fold per table. The aux natural-key case-duplicate scan
  (governance-vote twin pattern + bridge_validators) runs in the same pass.
- The driver now digests the fleet-COMMON PREFIX: pass one reads each node's
  sealed height, pass two bounds height-scoped tables (block.height,
  transaction.block_height, *_history.applied_height — NULL applied_height
  means in-force and stays in) to the fleet minimum. Without the bound the
  proposer being one block ahead read as a block/transaction consensus FAIL
  on every run — pure sampling timing, not drift.

Auxiliary upsert case fix:
- aux_state.py upsert_aux_rows matched all natural-key fields with exact
  equality — a checksummed incoming voter_address did not match the stored
  lowercase row and inserted a twin. Address-bearing key fields now compare
