### Correction: the 2026-08-05 "verification" pass was wrong

An earlier revision of this file claimed 15 of the highest-severity findings were
**fabricated** — that they cited code which did not exist. That claim was false and has
been withdrawn.

The verification ran at ~15:00 on 2026-08-05 against a working tree that already
contained the AITBC-72/74/76 remediation landed between 2026-08-04 23:45 and
2026-08-05 12:14. It read the *fixed* code, found the defect absent, and concluded the
finding had been invented. Every one of the 15 has a matching remediation commit that
predates the check:

